@/************************ The routine _sin follows **********************

Name:           _sin
		[sin.s - sin.o]

Synopsis:       Implementation of the sine function of an argument X
		between -PI/2 and PI/2.

Performance and Memory Requirement:

	Instruction cycles:     38 with BMU device [Call & return included].
				38 with non BMU device [Call & return incl.].

	Code:                   20 words of ROM with BMU device.
				20 words of ROM with non BMU device.

	Coefficients:           5 words of RAM.
	Local variables:        0 RAM locations.
	Static variables:       0
	Registers used: x, y, p, a0, a1, ar1, r0, auc
			auc is initialized to 0x0 [no scaling of p register].
	Accuracy:       Result is accurate to 16 bits of precision for
			inputs in the segment [-PI/2, PI/2].
Description:

	Algorithm: Sin(X) = X(c1+X^2(c3+X^2(c5+X^2(c7+X^2(c9)))))
		   where cn corresponds to coefficients of the Taylor
		   series expansion of the cosine function.

	BEGIN _sin
	    Set auc = 0
	    Angle X is passed via the a1h register in q14 format.
	    Compute nested polynomial series representation of sin(X).
	    Return result in a0h in q14 format.
	END _sin

Inputs:         The argument X, is passed in a0h in Q14 format.

Outputs:        The  sine of the argument is returned in a0h in q14 format.

Routines Called:        None.

This _sin routine was written by Homayoon Sam (March 1994) to run on
DSP1616. I evaluated and verified the routine efficiency on DSP1610,
included a performance summary, and added comments to the existing code
for clarification.

This routine shows 61.6% improvement in instruction cycles and 76.2%
improvement in memory requirements when BMU device is used and compared
to the performance on DSP16A.
Work by Aristos Nkansa-Kissi (Summer 1994).
***************************************************************************/
/*                                                                        */
#include <1610.h>               /* Include 16xx device header file.       */

.global _sin                    /* Declare routine as global. This allows */
				/* _sin to be called from other routines. */
.rsect ".ram"                   /* Assemble in .ram.                      */

_sin:   auc = 0x0               /* No scaling of p register.              */
	x=a1                    /* Load input number into x, in q14.      */
	y=a1                    /* Load input number into y, in q14.      */
	p=x*y                   /* Calcualte x^2 in q12.                  */
	a0=p                    /* Load x^2 into a0, retain q12 format.   */
	x=a0                    /* Load x^2 into x reg.                   */
	auc=0x02                /* Load p<<2 into a0.                     */
	r0=SineCoeff            /* Pointer to sine coefficients.          */
	y=*r0++                 /* Load the last coefficient cn into y.   */

do 4 {
	p=x*y  a0=*r0++         /* p gets x^2 * c[n], a0 gets c[n-1].     */
	a0 = a0+p               /* a0 gets c[n-1] + x^2 * a[n].           */
	y = a0
     }                          /* This is two cycles.                    */

	x=a1                    /* Restore original x value (input).      */
	p=x*y                   /* p now has sine(x).                     */
	a0=p                    /* a0=sin(x) in q14 format.              */

	return

.rsect ".ram"                   /* Begin assembly in RAM.                 */

SineCoeff:              /*****  all numbers in q14 format by default  *****/
	int 0.000705467         /* c9<<8 */
	int -0.0126984          /* c7<<6 */
	int 0.133333            /* c5<<4 */
	int -0.666667           /* c3<<2 */
	int 1.0                 /* c1 */

/***********************************************************************/

@


